    "customfield_12311020": null,
    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12497640/comment/12990379",
          "id": "12990379",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Patch.\n\nLogMP now skips any segments that are currently being merged (when requireContiguous is false).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-02-03T23:40:43.784+0000",
          "updated": "2011-02-03T23:40:43.784+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12497640/comment/13029403",
          "id": "13029403",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I think we should simply change the API for MergePolicy.\nInstead of SegmentInfos it should accept a Set<SegmentInfo> with SIs eligible for merging (eg, completely written & not elected for another merge).\nIW.getMergingSegments() is a damn cheat, and \"Expert\" notice is not an excuse! :)\nWhy should each and every MP do the set substraction when IW can do it for them once and for all? ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-05T16:07:27.979+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-05T16:07:27.979+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12497640/comment/13029408",
          "id": "13029408",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Ok, I'm wrong. We need both a list of all SIs and eligible SIs for calculations. But that should be handled through API change, not a new public method on IW.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-05-05T16:13:48.755+0000",
          "updated": "2011-05-05T16:13:48.755+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12497640/comment/13029435",
          "id": "13029435",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Earwin, that sounds great (changing current API instead of new IW method), I think?  Can you open a new issue?  Thanks.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
